# Experiment artifacts (CLAUDE.md §4 / experiments-rules.md §5):
# runs/<EXP-ID>/ holds per-experiment ckpt / eval / tb / snapshot;
# all PHI-bearing intermediates (CSV rows containing mention/context) stay
# here and never enter git. Numeric metrics may be force-added (`git add -f`)
# on a case-by-case basis if they contain no PHI.
runs/
logs/slurm/

# papers/ is mostly large binaries (LaTeX build artifacts, PDFs, docx, zipped
# annotation data with potential PHI). Only allow specific text artifacts in
# the BMJ Revision response folder to enter git.
papers/*
!papers/BMJ_AI_Submission/
papers/BMJ_AI_Submission/*
!papers/BMJ_AI_Submission/Major Revision/
papers/BMJ_AI_Submission/Major Revision/*
!papers/BMJ_AI_Submission/Major Revision/*.md
!papers/BMJ_AI_Submission/Major Revision/*.txt
!papers/BMJ_AI_Submission/Major Revision/cross-annotation/
papers/BMJ_AI_Submission/Major Revision/cross-annotation/*
!papers/BMJ_AI_Submission/Major Revision/cross-annotation/*.txt
